WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.122
Walt grew up in the small town of Marceline, Missouri.

2
00:00:08.123 --> 00:00:11.582
From an early age he loved to draw.

3
00:00:11.583 --> 00:00:17.538
He first made money from his art when he was a boy.

4
00:00:17.539 --> 00:00:23.302
A neighbor paid Walt to draw a picture of his horse.

5
00:00:23.303 --> 00:00:26.420
Walt also loved to read.

6
00:00:26.421 --> 00:00:30.600
His favorite book was The Adventures of Tom Sawyer

7
00:00:30.601 --> 00:00:37.977
. He imagined having adventures like

8
00:00:37.978 --> 00:00:42.475
Tom. Walking to school one day, Walt saw a

9
00:00:42.476 --> 00:00:45.566
poster. It advertised a

10
00:00:45.567 --> 00:00:50.703
play. "It's a play about a boy who can fly," he said to his brother,

11
00:00:50.704 --> 00:00:54.583
Roy. "Let's ask Mom if we can go."

12
00:00:54.584 --> 00:00:59.045
"Can we go see Peter Pan ?" Walt asked his

13
00:00:59.046 --> 00:01:05.229
mom. "As long as you pay for your tickets, sure," she

14
00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:08.967
said. Walt and Roy gathered money to buy two

15
00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:14.239
tickets. Walt especially was amazed by the

16
00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:19.764
play. Shortly afterward the boys' school put on the same

17
00:01:19.765 --> 00:01:24.846
play. Walt got to play the role of Peter

18
00:01:24.847 --> 00:01:31.178
Pan. He asked Roy to help him fly during the

19
00:01:31.179 --> 00:01:35.642
play. "Don't be silly. You can't fly," Roy

20
00:01:35.643 --> 00:01:39.848
said. But Walt convinced Roy to help

21
00:01:39.849 --> 00:01:48.519
him. They found some strong rope for a pulley

22
00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:59.944
system. Crash! Bang! Ouch! Finally Walt rose into the

23
00:01:59.945 --> 00:02:04.904
air. "Look at me! I'm flying!" he

24
00:02:04.905 --> 00:02:08.587
shouted. "That was so neat," Roy said

25
00:02:08.588 --> 00:02:12.044
later. "I hope we can both be in the movies when we grow

26
00:02:12.045 --> 00:02:15.497
up." "I hope so," Walt

27
00:02:15.498 --> 00:02:20.058
answered. Later the family moved to Kansas City,

28
00:02:20.059 --> 00:02:25.814
Missouri. Walt and Roy got a job delivering

29
00:02:25.815 --> 00:02:31.488
newspapers. They had to wake up at 4:30 a.m. every

30
00:02:31.489 --> 00:02:36.720
morning. That was hard, but Walt used the money for the

31
00:02:36.721 --> 00:02:39.647
movies! He loved to watch

32
00:02:39.648 --> 00:02:43.805
movies. And he still loved to draw.

33
00:02:43.806 --> 00:02:47.827
Most of all he liked to make people laugh.

34
00:02:47.828 --> 00:02:51.853
His teacher predicted he would become an actor.

35
00:02:51.854 --> 00:02:55.327
Walt Disney did not become an actor.

36
00:02:55.328 --> 00:03:00.151
Instead he became an animator.

37
00:03:00.152 --> 00:03:05.552
Animating combined his interest in movies with his talent for drawing.

38
00:03:05.553 --> 00:03:09.108
He never forgot Peter Pan though.

39
00:03:09.109 --> 00:03:14.942
In 1953 he even produced his own animated version of it.

40
00:03:14.943 --> 00:03:19.135
Walt began as a small-town boy who loved to draw.

41
00:03:19.136 --> 00:03:24.149
He went on to become a famous creator of animated movies.

42
00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:35.132
Even today his movies bring joy to children all around the world.

